      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's crucial to protect your privacy, especially when dealing with biometric data. While using the chair, you might explore options like routinely covering the sensors with your clothing, turning off any data-sharing settings, or even physically blocking the sensors using light objects, if permissible. Finally, you could regularly inquire about any settings that might allow you to disable such data collection when not in use. However, if your concerns persist, please discuss your discomfort and privacy with your company's IT department or the chair's manufacturer.",
