      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the ideas. i'm really worried about the micro-movements part though. if it's tracking breathing patterns or tiny muscle twitches to gauge my focus, a cushion might not be enough. is there anything else i can wear or use that would interfere with bio-electrical signals or the way these sensors pick up on movement? like, would something like a weighted lap pad or even certain types of heavy fabric help mask my actual biometric signature?",
